---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Grossline — the monthly report"
  description="What's in the Grossline monthly report: headline, blended efficiency, margin, claim gap, what changed, and the findings worth acting on."
  path="/the-report"
  wide
>
  <h1>The monthly report</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The same shape every month, so you know where to look without reading. Consistency is the
    product.
  </p>

  <h2>Every report, in order</h2>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="card"><h3>Headline</h3><p>One sentence: whether the month worked, the contribution figure, and the direction of travel.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Blended efficiency</h3><p>MER against break-even and target; blended CAC against first-order contribution.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Margin</h3><p>The waterfall from gross sales to contribution, with cost completeness stated.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Channel &amp; claim gap</h3><p>Spend by platform, platform-claimed against store-recorded — shown as measurement, not correction.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>What changed</h3><p>Month over month and year over year on the headline metrics, absent where history does not exist.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Findings &amp; checks</h3><p>Up to three findings in a four-part shape, plus what we will check next month and how last month's turned out.</p></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Read a real one</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    A prospect who reads a real report understands the product completely. This one is generated by
    the same pipeline your report would be.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a class="btn" href="/sample-report.pdf">Download the sample report (PDF)</a>
  </p>
  <p class="demo-note">
    Generated from a demo tenant with realistic seeded data — not a real merchant's numbers.
  </p>
</Base>
